      "text": "To determine how many books are left over after repacking them into boxes of 40, we first need to find the remainder when 1335 is divided by 40.\n\n1. **Calculate the number of full boxes in the first repacking:**\n\n   Given:\n   \\[\n   1335 \\text{ books}\n   \\]\n   We want to repack them into boxes of 40.\n\n   Let \\( x \\) be the number of full boxes:\n   \\[\n   x = \\left\\lfloor \\frac{1335}{40} \\right\\rfloor\n   \\]\n\n   Perform the division:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{1335}{40} = 33.375\n   \\]\n\n   Taking the floor value, \\( x \\) becomes:\n   \\[\n   x = \\left\\lfloor 33.375 \\right\\rfloor = 33\n   \\]\n\n   Therefore, Melvin can pack 33 full boxes, each containing 40 books.\n\n2. **Calculate the number of books used so far:**\n\n   Since each full box contains 40 books:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Books used} = 33 \\times 40 = 1320\n   \\]\n\n3. **Calculate the number of books left over:**\n\n   Subtract the number of books used from the total number of books:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Books left over} = 1335 - 1320 = 15\n   \\]\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{15}\n\\]",
