      "text": "To determine how many books Melvin has left over after packing them into boxes with 40 books each, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Calculate the total number of books by multiplying the number of boxes by the number of books per box.\n2. Divide the total number of books by 40 to find out how many full boxes can be made and how many books are left over.\n\nLet's start by calculating the total number of books:\n\n\\[ 1335 \\text{ boxes} \\times 39 \\text{ books per box} \\]\n\nThen, we will determine the remainder:\n\n\\[ \\text{Total books mod } 40 \\]\n\nWe'll use Python to perform these calculations accurately.\n```python\n# Step 1: Calculate the total number of books\nboxes = 1335\nbooks_per_box = 39\n\ntotal_books = boxes * books_per_box\n\n# Step 2: Calculate the remainder when the total number of books is divided by 40\nbooks_left_over = total_books % 40\nprint((total_books, books_left_over))\n```\n```output\n(52105, 5)\n```\nThe total number of books Melvin has is \\( 52105 \\). After repacking them into boxes with 40 books each, the number of books left over is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{5}\n\\]",
